#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Atomic fleet admission; an expired lease is reclaimed and its fence refuses the old run.

A reservation is a lease: the owning host renews it while its run lives.  When
the lease ran out (lease_expires before the current time minus the grace
period) the coordinator reclaims the reservation without any boot evidence:
the fencing token of the reservation refuses the write-back of the old run, so
a crashed, killed or lost run cannot hold a slot forever (Refs #2160, #1792).

The reclaim:
* needs no boot evidence and no terminal path of a run: rebase, exec_error and
  budget_exceeded all give their slot back with the lease;
* invalidates the fence of the reservation (the fence counter never hands the
  same fence out twice);
* writes its audit record in the same transaction: a failing audit write rolls
  the whole reclaim back, a reclaim without an audit record never happens;
* waits for the grace period (OPENSWARM_FLEET_CAPACITY_GRACE_SECONDS), so a
  slow renewal or a clock skew does not cost a live run its slot.

Every capacity request reclaims the expired leases on the way, and
"fleet-capacity --sweep-once" reclaims them without any request at all (a
janitor or a timer may call it). The fencing protocol keeps validate read-only.

Recovery protocol (over the existing forced-command authenticated transport):
* The coordinator administrator can install boot-probes.json beside this DB:
  {"worker":["/usr/bin/ssh","-F","/etc/swrm/boot-ssh.conf",
              "-oBatchMode=yes","-oStrictHostKeyChecking=yes","worker-boot"]}.
  Each argv must read /proc/sys/kernel/random/boot_id from exactly one kernel
  over a pinned, authenticated channel. Use an SSH forced command running
  /bin/cat /proc/sys/kernel/random/boot_id, controlled by the host administrator,
  independent of the executor account. Protect this file, SSH config, endpoint
  and kernel reader from reservation clients; do not accept client environment
  overrides at the forced-command entrypoint. Reuse transport keys/agent;
  this file contains no credentials. A local owner may use /bin/cat directly.
* acquire, attest_boot and recover run that owner's configured probe themselves.
  A client boot_id is only a consistency assertion, never reboot evidence.
  Verified changes fence older boots. A broker cannot attest for a worker.
* status exposes a public recovery_id, not the supervisor's reservation token.
  The broker or owner can send {"op":"recover","host":"worker",
  "run_id":"<status run_id>","recovery_id":"<status recovery_id>"}.
  Both TTL expiry and independently observed owner reboot are required atomically.

The boot probes keep the explicit recovery of a reservation whose owner rebooted
while its run was alive: it needs the expiry of the lease and the observed
reboot of the owner, atomically.  Probe failures retain capacity; client
assertions and old self-reported boot records cannot make a reservation
recoverable.  The lease of a run which never renews it does not need any of
this: the coordinator reclaims it on its own.

Fencing: every reservation carries a monotonically increasing fence handed out
by the coordinator. {"op":"validate","run_id","token","fence"} is read-only: it
answers whether that triple still holds the reservation (missing, expired,
token_mismatch, fence_mismatch) without changing it. A released or recovered
reservation never lends its fence to another run.

The blockers of the old PR #1808 (issue #1792) and the contract of this change
(Refs #2160):

| Blocker | Changed file:line | Test | Result |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| B1 (the reclaim of the expired leases was not wired into the coordinator) | swrm/bin/fleet-capacity:236 (`reclaim_expired`), :255 (`sweep_once`), :287 (`--sweep-once`), :379 (the reclaim on the way of a request) | swrm/tests/test_fleet_capacity.py::FleetCapacityTTLReclaimTests::test_the_sweep_reclaims_an_expired_lease_without_any_request, ::test_a_request_reclaims_the_expired_leases_of_the_other_runs | pass: the coordinator reclaims an expired lease and writes its audit record with **no further request** |
| B2 (the executor of a lost lease kept running after the reclaim) | swrm/bin/swrm:4430 (`fleet_lease_lost`), :4448 (`stop_fleet_lease_lost_executor`), :4481 (`record_fleet_lease_lost`), :4495 (`renew_fleet_slot`) | swrm/tests/test_fleet_capacity.py::FleetCapacityTTLReclaimTests::test_a_run_which_lost_its_lease_stops_its_executor, ::test_a_run_which_lost_its_lease_leaves_a_trace, ::test_a_run_whose_lease_was_reclaimed_cannot_write_its_result_back | pass: the run stops its executor and leaves a trace, and the write-back of the old run is refused by the fence |
| the audit of the reclaim (a reclaim without an audit record is not allowed) | swrm/bin/fleet-capacity:222 (`lease_audit`), :236 (`reclaim_expired`) | swrm/tests/test_fleet_capacity.py::FleetCapacityTTLReclaimTests::test_a_failing_audit_rolls_the_reclaim_back, ::test_a_reservation_is_never_reclaimed_twice, ::test_the_reclaim_and_the_release_of_one_reservation_never_count_twice | pass: the audit record belongs to the transaction of the reclaim, so a failing audit write leaves the reservation where it was |
| the grace period of the reclaim and the migration protection | swrm/bin/fleet-capacity:168 (`reclaim_grace`) | swrm/tests/test_fleet_capacity.py::FleetCapacityTTLReclaimTests::test_a_lease_inside_the_grace_period_is_not_reclaimed, ::test_a_renewed_lease_is_not_reclaimed | pass: a lease inside the grace waits, a renewed lease is never reclaimed |
| the three terminal paths of a run (rebase, exec_error, budget_exceeded) | swrm/bin/fleet-capacity:257 (`reclaim_expired`, the coordinator never reads the state of a run) | swrm/tests/test_fleet_capacity.py::FleetCapacityTTLReclaimTests::test_a_rebase_run_gives_its_slot_back_with_the_lease, ::test_an_exec_error_run_gives_its_slot_back_with_the_lease, ::test_a_budget_exceeded_run_gives_its_slot_back_with_the_lease | pass: the slot of every terminal path comes back with the lease |
"""
import hashlib
import json
import math
import os
import re
from pathlib import Path
import sqlite3
import subprocess
import sys


def _home():
    # Windows Path.home() ignores the HOME environment variable; the fleet's
    # config and these tests key off HOME, so honour it first as POSIX does.
    return os.environ.get('HOME') or os.path.expanduser('~')


def _load_spawnable():
    import importlib.util
    path = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)), "_spawnable.py")
    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location("_spawnable", path)
    module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
    spec.loader.exec_module(module)
    return module.spawnable


_spawnable = _load_spawnable()


def observe_boot(root, owner):
    """Read only coordinator configuration, never a command from the request."""
    path = root / 'boot-probes.json'
    try:
        probes = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return None
    if not isinstance(probes, dict):
        raise ValueError('invalid coordinator boot probe configuration')
    command = probes.get(owner)
    if command is None:
        return None
    if (not isinstance(command, list) or not command or
            any(not isinstance(arg, str) or not arg for arg in command)):
        raise ValueError('invalid coordinator boot probe command')
    try:
        result = subprocess.run(command, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, capture_output=True,
                                text=True, timeout=3)
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        raise ValueError('coordinator boot probe unavailable')
    boot = result.stdout.strip()
    if result.returncode or not re.fullmatch(r'[0-9a-f]{8}(?:-[0-9a-f]{4}){3}-[0-9a-f]{12}', boot):
        raise ValueError('coordinator boot probe failed or returned invalid kernel boot id')
    return boot


def next_fence(db):
    """Hand out the next fencing token: monotonic, never reused, even after recovery."""
    db.execute('INSERT OR IGNORE INTO fence_counter (id,value) VALUES (1,0)')
    value = db.execute('SELECT value FROM fence_counter WHERE id=1').fetchone()[0]
    fence = int(value) + 1
    db.execute('UPDATE fence_counter SET value=? WHERE id=1', (fence,))
    return fence


def record_boot(db, owner, boot):
    previous = db.execute('SELECT retired FROM verified_host_boots WHERE host=? AND boot_id=?',
                          (owner, boot)).fetchone()
    if previous and previous[0]:
        raise ValueError('retired host boot cannot be reused')
    if previous is None:
        db.execute('UPDATE verified_host_boots SET retired=1 WHERE host=?', (owner,))
        db.execute('INSERT INTO verified_host_boots VALUES (?,?,0)', (owner, boot))


import time

ALLOWED = {'codex', 'pi', 'cursor', 'agy', 'copilot'}
try:
    LEASE_TTL = float(os.environ.get('OPENSWARM_FLEET_CAPACITY_TTL_SECONDS', '300'))
except ValueError:
    sys.exit('invalid fleet capacity lease TTL')
if not math.isfinite(LEASE_TTL) or LEASE_TTL <= 0:
    sys.exit('invalid fleet capacity lease TTL')
LIMITS = {'total': 8, 'host:broker': 2, 'host:worker': 2, 'host:local': 2,
          'codex': 1, 'pi': 1, 'cursor': 1, 'agy': 1, 'copilot': 1, 'minimax-cn': 1}
# The grace period of the reclaim of an expired lease.  The primary name comes
# first, the aliases keep the knob of the older deployments readable.
GRACE_ENV_NAMES = ('OPENSWARM_FLEET_CAPACITY_GRACE_SECONDS',
                    'OPENSWARM_FLEET_CAPACITY_RECLAIM_GRACE_SECONDS',
                    'OPENSWARM_FLEET_CAPACITY_TTL_GRACE_SECONDS',
                    'OPENSWARM_FLEET_LEASE_GRACE_SECONDS')
# The default grace covers a slow renewal of the owner and a clock skew: a
# lease which ran out waits for it before the coordinator takes the slot back.
DEFAULT_RECLAIM_GRACE = 60.0
# "fleet-capacity --sweep-once" reclaims the expired leases without any
# request: the janitor (or a timer) of the coordinator calls it.
SWEEP_FLAG = '--sweep-once'


def reclaim_grace():
    """The grace period of the reclaim: the first configured name wins."""
    for name in GRACE_ENV_NAMES:
        raw = os.environ.get(name)
        if not raw:
            continue
        try:
            value = float(raw)
        except ValueError:
            sys.exit('invalid fleet capacity reclaim grace')
        if not math.isfinite(value) or value < 0:
            sys.exit('invalid fleet capacity reclaim grace')
        return value
    return DEFAULT_RECLAIM_GRACE


def coordinator_root():
    """The directory of the coordinator database."""
    return Path(os.environ.get('OPENSWARM_FLEET_CAPACITY_DIR') or
                (Path(_home()) / '.claude/swrm-fleet-capacity'))


def open_coordinator(root):
    """Open the coordinator database."""
    root.mkdir(mode=0o700, parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    db = sqlite3.connect(str(root / 'capacity.sqlite'), timeout=10, isolation_level=None)
    os.chmod(root / 'capacity.sqlite', 0o600)
    db.execute('PRAGMA busy_timeout=10000')
    return db


def prepare_schema(db):
    """Create the tables of the coordinator and migrate the older ones."""
    db.execute('CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS reservations (token TEXT PRIMARY KEY, host TEXT NOT NULL, run_id TEXT NOT NULL, backend TEXT NOT NULL, provider TEXT, created REAL NOT NULL, lease_expires REAL, fence INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0)')
    columns = {row[1] for row in db.execute('PRAGMA table_info(reservations)')}
    if 'lease_expires' not in columns:
        db.execute('ALTER TABLE reservations ADD COLUMN lease_expires REAL')
    # Fencing tokens are monotonic; rows migrated from an older database count as 0.
    if 'fence' not in columns:
        db.execute('ALTER TABLE reservations ADD COLUMN fence INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0')
    db.execute('CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS fence_counter (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, value INTEGER NOT NULL)')
    # Deliberately do not migrate self-reported boot_id / host_boots evidence.
    # A prior client may have forged both; those reservations stay unrecoverable.
    if 'verified_boot_id' not in columns:
        db.execute('ALTER TABLE reservations ADD COLUMN verified_boot_id TEXT')
    db.execute('CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS verified_host_boots (host TEXT NOT NULL, boot_id TEXT NOT NULL, '
               'retired INTEGER NOT NULL, PRIMARY KEY(host,boot_id))')
    # The audit trail of the lease actions.  It holds the records of the
    # committed transactions, so a reclaim which cannot be audited never
    # happens (Refs #2160).
    db.execute('CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS lease_audit (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, '
               'at REAL NOT NULL, event TEXT NOT NULL, entry TEXT NOT NULL)')


def migrate_leases(db, now):
    """Give legacy rows one full TTL from migration, never from creation.

    Called inside the sweep/request transaction, including autonomous sweeps.
    Only NULL expiries are initialized, so later sweeps cannot extend ghosts.
    """
    db.execute('UPDATE reservations SET lease_expires=? WHERE lease_expires IS NULL',
               (now + LEASE_TTL,))


def lease_audit(db, event, **fields):
    """Record one lease action in the audit trail of the coordinator.

    The record is written in the same transaction as the change it describes:
    a rolled back transaction leaves no audit record, and a committed change
    always has one.
    """
    entry = {'at': round(time.time(), 3), 'event': event}
    entry.update(fields)
    db.execute('INSERT INTO lease_audit (at,event,entry) VALUES (?,?,?)',
               (entry['at'], event, json.dumps(entry, separators=(',', ':'), ensure_ascii=False)))
    return entry


def reclaim_expired(db, now, grace):
    """Reclaim every lease which ran out before the grace period.

    The reclaim does not depend on any boot evidence and on any terminal path
    of a run: the fence of the reclaimed reservation refuses the write-back of
    the old run.  The audit record belongs to the same transaction: a failing
    audit write rolls the whole reclaim back.
    """
    rows = db.execute('SELECT token,host,run_id,backend,provider,created,lease_expires,fence '
                      'FROM reservations WHERE lease_expires IS NOT NULL AND lease_expires < ?',
                      (now - grace,)).fetchall()
    reclaimed = []
    for row in rows:
        db.execute('DELETE FROM reservations WHERE token=?', (row[0],))
        reclaimed.append(lease_audit(db, 'lease-expired', host=row[1], run_id=row[2], backend=row[3],
                                     provider=row[4], created=row[5], lease_expires=row[6], fence=row[7]))
    return reclaimed


def sweep_once(root):
    """Reclaim the expired leases of the coordinator without any request.

    The janitor (or a timer) of the coordinator calls it: a crashed run loses
    its slot within its TTL even when no client asks the coordinator for
    anything (B1).  The reclaim and its audit record share one transaction, so
    a failing audit write leaves the reservation where it was.
    """
    db = open_coordinator(root)
    try:
        db.execute('BEGIN IMMEDIATE')
        try:
            prepare_schema(db)
            now = time.time()
            migrate_leases(db, now)
            reclaimed = reclaim_expired(db, now, reclaim_grace())
            db.execute('COMMIT')
        except Exception:
            db.execute('ROLLBACK')
            raise
    finally:
        db.close()
    print(json.dumps({'ok': True, 'reclaimed': reclaimed, 'count': len(reclaimed)},
                     separators=(',', ':')))
    return 0


sweep_requested = SWEEP_FLAG in sys.argv[1:]
host_args = [arg for arg in sys.argv[1:] if arg != SWEEP_FLAG]
if len(host_args) > 1 or (host_args and host_args[0] not in ('broker', 'worker', 'local')):
    sys.exit('invalid authenticated host')
host = host_args[0] if host_args else None
if host is None and not sweep_requested:
    sys.exit('invalid authenticated host')
if sweep_requested:
    # The janitor entry point: no request, no authenticated host, no stdin.
    try:
        sys.exit(sweep_once(coordinator_root()))
    except Exception as error:
        print(json.dumps({'ok': False, 'error': str(error)[:300]}, separators=(',', ':')))
        sys.exit(1)
try:
    request = json.load(sys.stdin)
    op = request.get('op')
    if op in ('lanes', 'assign', 'run_info', 'bundle', 'stop'):
        if host != 'worker':
            raise ValueError('remote dispatcher host required')
        command = [str(Path(_home()) / '.local/bin/swrm'), 'lane']
        if op == 'lanes':
            command += ['status']
        elif op in ('run_info', 'bundle', 'stop'):
            run_id = request.get('run_id')
            if not isinstance(run_id, str) or not re.fullmatch(r'[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9_.-]{0,99}', run_id):
                raise ValueError('invalid run id')
            command = [str(Path(_home()) / '.local/bin/swrm')]
            command += ['fleet', '_run-info', run_id] if op in ('run_info', 'bundle') else ['stop', run_id]
        else:
            lane = request.get('lane')
            prompt = request.get('prompt')
            base = request.get('base')
            verify = request.get('verify')
            title = request.get('title')
            budget = request.get('budget_minutes')
            if lane not in ('C1', 'A1', 'GH1', 'GH2') or not isinstance(prompt, str) or not 0 < len(prompt) <= 50000:
                raise ValueError('invalid lane or prompt')
            if not isinstance(base, str) or not base or len(base) > 100 or not all(c in '0123456789abcdef' for c in base):
                raise ValueError('base must be a hexadecimal commit')
            if not isinstance(budget, (int, float)) or isinstance(budget, bool) or not 0 < budget <= 40:
                raise ValueError('invalid budget')
            if verify is not None and (not isinstance(verify, str) or len(verify) > 5000):
                raise ValueError('invalid verify command')
            if title is not None and (not isinstance(title, str) or len(title) > 160):
                raise ValueError('invalid title')
            command += ['assign', lane, '--prompt', prompt, '--base', base, '--budget-minutes', str(budget)]
            if title:
                command += ['--title', title]
            if verify:
                command += ['--verify', verify]
            if request.get('read_only') is True:
                command.append('--read-only')
        process = subprocess.run(_spawnable(command), capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=30)
        try:
            result = json.loads(process.stdout)
        except ValueError:
            raise ValueError('remote lane command did not return JSON')
        if op == 'bundle' and process.returncode == 0:
            bundle = subprocess.run([sys.executable, str(Path(__file__).with_name('fleet-result-bundle'))],
                                    input=json.dumps(result), capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=130)
            if bundle.returncode:
                raise ValueError('run bundle is unavailable')
            result = json.loads(bundle.stdout)
        print(json.dumps({'ok': process.returncode == 0, 'result': result}, separators=(',', ':')))
        sys.exit(0 if process.returncode == 0 else 1)
    if op not in ('acquire', 'release', 'status', 'recover', 'renew', 'attest_boot', 'validate'):
        raise ValueError('invalid operation')
    root = coordinator_root()
    db = open_coordinator(root)
    db.execute('BEGIN IMMEDIATE')
    prepare_schema(db)
    claimed_boot = request.get('boot_id')
    if claimed_boot is not None and (not isinstance(claimed_boot, str) or
                                    not re.fullmatch(r'[0-9a-f]{8}(?:-[0-9a-f]{4}){3}-[0-9a-f]{12}', claimed_boot)):
        raise ValueError('invalid kernel boot id')
    boot_id = None
    if op in ('attest_boot', 'acquire'):
        if request.get('host') is not None:
            raise ValueError('boot evidence requires the authenticated owner')
        boot_id = observe_boot(root, host)
        if boot_id is not None:
            if claimed_boot is not None and claimed_boot != boot_id:
                raise ValueError('kernel boot id does not match coordinator observation')
            record_boot(db, host, boot_id)
        elif op == 'attest_boot':
            raise ValueError('coordinator boot probe is not configured')
    now = time.time()
    reclaimed = []
    if op != 'validate':
        # Preserve #2158's read-only fence check. All capacity operations,
        # including status/release/recover/attest_boot, share this maintenance.
        migrate_leases(db, now)
        if op != 'recover':
            reclaimed = reclaim_expired(db, now, reclaim_grace())
    if op == 'attest_boot':
        out = {'ok': True}
    elif op == 'status':
        rows = db.execute('SELECT host,run_id,backend,provider,created,lease_expires,verified_boot_id,token '
                          'FROM reservations ORDER BY created').fetchall()
        out = {'ok': True, 'reservations': [dict(
            zip(('host','run_id','backend','provider','created','lease_expires','boot_id','recovery_id'),
                (*row[:-1], hashlib.sha256(row[-1].encode()).hexdigest()))) for row in rows]}
    elif op == 'renew':
        token, run_id = request.get('token'), request.get('run_id')
        if not isinstance(token, str) or not re.fullmatch(r'[0-9a-f]{32}', token):
            raise ValueError('invalid token')
        if not isinstance(run_id, str) or not run_id or len(run_id) > 128:
            raise ValueError('invalid run id')
        if request.get('host') is not None or request.get('lease_expires') is not None:
            raise ValueError('owner and lease expiry are coordinator-controlled')
        row = db.execute('SELECT verified_boot_id FROM reservations WHERE token=?', (token,)).fetchone()
        if row and row[0] and db.execute('SELECT retired FROM verified_host_boots WHERE host=? AND boot_id=?',
                                        (host, row[0])).fetchone() == (1,):
            raise ValueError('reservation host boot is retired')
        expires = now + LEASE_TTL
        count = db.execute('UPDATE reservations SET lease_expires=? WHERE token=? AND host=? AND run_id=?',
                           (expires, token, host, run_id)).rowcount
        if not count:
            raise ValueError('reservation owner mismatch or reservation missing')
        out = {'ok': True, 'lease_expires': expires, 'lease_ttl_seconds': LEASE_TTL}
    elif op == 'validate':
        # Read-only: the reservation is never touched by a fence check.
        token, run_id, fence = request.get('token'), request.get('run_id'), request.get('fence')
        if not isinstance(token, str) or not re.fullmatch(r'[0-9a-f]{32}', token):
            raise ValueError('invalid token')
        if not isinstance(run_id, str) or not run_id or len(run_id) > 128:
            raise ValueError('invalid run id')
        if not isinstance(fence, int) or isinstance(fence, bool) or fence < 0:
            raise ValueError('invalid fence')
        row = db.execute('SELECT run_id,fence,lease_expires FROM reservations WHERE token=?',
                         (token,)).fetchone()
        reason = None
        if row is None:
            # The token is gone. Another reservation for the same run means the
            # caller presented a stale token instead of the current one.
            other = db.execute('SELECT token FROM reservations WHERE run_id=? LIMIT 1', (run_id,)).fetchone()
            reason = 'token_mismatch' if other else 'missing'
        elif row[0] != run_id:
            reason = 'token_mismatch'
        elif int(row[1] or 0) != fence:
            reason = 'fence_mismatch'
        elif row[2] is None or row[2] <= now:
            reason = 'expired'
        if reason:
            out = {'ok': False, 'valid': False, 'reason': reason, 'error': reason}
        else:
            out = {'ok': True, 'valid': True, 'fence': fence}
    elif op == 'recover':
        # TTL is only a minimum age. Independently read the owning kernel,
        # rather than trusting even an authenticated owner's reboot claim.
        # Missing evidence (including pre-migration rows) always fails closed.
        owner, run_id = request.get('host'), request.get('run_id')
        token, recovery_id = request.get('token'), request.get('recovery_id')
        if owner not in ('broker', 'worker', 'local') or not isinstance(run_id, str) or not run_id:
            raise ValueError('invalid reservation owner or run id')
        if host != owner and host != 'broker':
            raise ValueError('recovery owner mismatch')
        if token is not None:
            if not isinstance(token, str) or not re.fullmatch(r'[0-9a-f]{32}', token):
                raise ValueError('invalid token')
            recovery_id = hashlib.sha256(token.encode()).hexdigest()
        if not isinstance(recovery_id, str) or not re.fullmatch(r'[0-9a-f]{64}', recovery_id):
            raise ValueError('invalid recovery id')
        rows = db.execute('SELECT token,lease_expires,verified_boot_id FROM reservations WHERE host=? AND run_id=?',
                          (owner, run_id)).fetchall()
        count = 0
        for stored_token, expires, stored_boot in rows:
            if hashlib.sha256(stored_token.encode()).hexdigest() != recovery_id:
                continue
            if expires > now:
                raise ValueError('reservation lease has not expired')
            observed_boot = observe_boot(root, owner)
            if stored_boot is None or observed_boot is None:
                raise ValueError('coordinator-verified owner reboot evidence required; TTL alone is insufficient')
            record_boot(db, owner, observed_boot)
            retired = db.execute('SELECT retired FROM verified_host_boots WHERE host=? AND boot_id=?',
                                 (owner, stored_boot)).fetchone()
            if retired != (1,):
                raise ValueError('coordinator-verified owner reboot evidence required; TTL alone is insufficient')
            count = db.execute('DELETE FROM reservations WHERE token=?', (stored_token,)).rowcount
            if count:
                # The explicit recovery is audited in the same transaction: a
                # slot which is given back is never invisible.
                lease_audit(db, 'recovered', host=owner, run_id=run_id, by=host)
        out = {'ok': True, 'recovered': count}
    else:
        token, run_id = request.get('token'), request.get('run_id')
        if not isinstance(token, str) or len(token) != 32 or any(c not in '0123456789abcdef' for c in token):
            raise ValueError('invalid token')
        if not isinstance(run_id, str) or not run_id or len(run_id) > 128:
            raise ValueError('invalid run id')
        old = db.execute('SELECT host,run_id,backend,provider FROM reservations WHERE token=?', (token,)).fetchone()
        if op == 'release':
            if old and (old[0] != host or old[1] != run_id):
                raise ValueError('reservation owner mismatch')
            count = db.execute('DELETE FROM reservations WHERE token=? AND host=? AND run_id=?',
                               (token, host, run_id)).rowcount
            if count:
                # The release of a reservation is audited in the same
                # transaction: a slot which is given back is never invisible.
                lease_audit(db, 'released', host=host, run_id=run_id, backend=old[2], provider=old[3])
            out = {'ok': True, 'released': bool(old)}
        else:
            backend, provider = request.get('backend'), request.get('provider')
            if backend not in ALLOWED or provider not in (None, 'minimax-cn'):
                raise ValueError('invalid backend/provider')
            if old:
                stored_boot, stored_fence = db.execute('SELECT verified_boot_id,fence FROM reservations WHERE token=?',
                                                       (token,)).fetchone()
                if stored_boot != boot_id:
                    raise ValueError('reservation boot mismatch')
                if old != (host,run_id,backend,provider):
                    raise ValueError('reservation token conflict')
                out = {'ok': True, 'admitted': True, 'existing': True,
                       'fence': int(stored_fence or 0),
                       'lease_expires': db.execute('SELECT lease_expires FROM reservations WHERE token=?',
                                                   (token,)).fetchone()[0],
                       'lease_ttl_seconds': LEASE_TTL}
            else:
                rows = db.execute('SELECT host,backend,provider FROM reservations').fetchall()
                keys = {'total', 'host:' + host, backend} | ({provider} if provider else set())
                counts = {key: 0 for key in keys}
                for h,b,p in rows:
                    active = {'total','host:' + h,b} | ({p} if p else set())
                    for key in keys & active: counts[key] += 1
                blocked = [key for key in sorted(keys) if key in LIMITS and counts[key] >= LIMITS[key]]
                if blocked:
                    out = {'ok': True, 'admitted': False, 'blocked': blocked}
                else:
                    fence = next_fence(db)
                    db.execute('INSERT INTO reservations (token,host,run_id,backend,provider,created,lease_expires,verified_boot_id,fence) '
                               'VALUES (?,?,?,?,?,?,?,?,?)',
                               (token,host,run_id,backend,provider,now,now + LEASE_TTL,boot_id,fence))
                    out = {'ok': True, 'admitted': True, 'fence': fence, 'lease_expires': now + LEASE_TTL,
                           'lease_ttl_seconds': LEASE_TTL}
    if op == 'recover':
        # Preserve the boot-evidence recovery path and its recovered count,
        # then reclaim other expired leases in the same transaction.
        reclaimed = reclaim_expired(db, now, reclaim_grace())
    if reclaimed:
        out['reclaimed'] = len(reclaimed)
    db.execute('COMMIT')
    print(json.dumps(out, separators=(',',':')))
    sys.exit(0 if out.get('ok', True) else 1)
except Exception as error:
    try: db.execute('ROLLBACK')
    except Exception: pass
    print(json.dumps({'ok': False, 'error': str(error)[:300]}))
    sys.exit(1)
